   T-FIG ENHANCED v3.13e by Eugene A. Zeak, Jr.       REGISTRATION $20.00
 * COMM INTERACTIVE TELIX TUTORIAL

   Update

   T-FIG is an interactive tutorial intended for use with the Telix comm 
   program.  It runs just like a script from within Telix.  T-FIG reads 
   the present configuration of TELIX and displays it in a textual 
   format.  You can make a dynamic configuration change and T-FIG will 
   pick it up and display the new configuration.
   
   T-FIG is designed with the beginner in mind.  It allows the new 
   TELIX user to have easy access to the configuration information 
   needed to make TELIX more easily used.  It's not necessary to 
   remember any commands to use T-FIG...it's completely automatic.
   
   In many cases the information you need for the most widely used 
   applications are explained in T-FIG.  Section 5: TIPS and HINTS 
   contains stuff that causes most new users problems.  If you have a 
   particular problem, it's most likely here.  If not, use the new 
   on-line documentation.
   

   T-FIG ENHANCED, now with ON-LINE DOCUMENTATION and SHELL:
   
   I can't even begin to count the times that I needed a tidbit of 
   information from the manual, exited TELIX, loaded TELIX.DOC into an 
   editor, List, Browse, etc., found what I needed, changed back to the 
   TELIX directory, and finally, reran TELIX.  Now, for those with lots 
   of memory, problems don't exist...but, they did for me...regardless of 
   the frustration!  T-FIG gets around that by providing TELIX quick 
   reference with ON-LINE DOCUMENTATION.

  Also, a new and useful feature of T-FIG is SHELL.  Users can now 
  shell to DOS while T-FIG is running.
